Android/bionic has no pthread_cancel(). CUPS's _cupsThreadCancel() wraps it but
that helper has NO callers anywhere in the 2.4.19 tree outside thread.c itself
(verified by grep), so making it a no-op on Android is safe and keeps the private
API symbol present. Scoped to __ANDROID__.

--- a/cups/thread.c
+++ b/cups/thread.c
@@ -165,7 +165,13 @@
 void
 _cupsThreadCancel(_cups_thread_t thread)/* I - Thread ID */
 {
+#  ifdef __ANDROID__
+  /* bionic has no pthread_cancel(); this helper is unused internally, so make
+   * it a no-op rather than fail to link. */
+  (void)thread;
+#  else
   pthread_cancel(thread);
+#  endif /* __ANDROID__ */
 }
 
 
